admin-archivos-remoto-configurado = bucket defined on the server; test the connection before use
admin-archivos-remoto-sin-configurar = configure the bucket and credentials on the server first
admin-archivos-comprobar = Test configured storage
admin-archivos-comprobando = Testing storage. Wait for the test to finish.
admin-archivos-reinicio-pendiente = Storage change pending restart. New uploads are disabled.
admin-archivos-confirmar-proveedor = Configure { $proveedor }? Changing providers disables uploads until you restart the server and enable them again. Changes are allowed only when there are no attachments. No files will be moved or deleted.
admin-archivos-proveedor-guardado = Storage configuration saved. Check the active and configured providers before enabling uploads.
admin-archivos-no-disponible = Uploads cannot be enabled. The HTTP service must be running and any storage change must have been applied by restarting.
admin-archivos-configuracion-invalida = Invalid configuration. The per-file limit must be 1 to 128 MiB and no greater than the pending quota, which must not exceed 256 MiB.
admin-archivos-configuracion-cambiada = Configuration changed since you opened this option. Open it again to review current values.
admin-archivos-cambio-bloqueado = Storage cannot change while attachments exist, including pending uploads. File migration requires a separate operation.
admin-archivos-limite-invalido = Enter a whole number of MiB within the indicated limits.
admin-archivos-guardado = File settings saved.
admin-archivos-comprobacion-correcta = Storage test passed: a temporary test file was written, read and deleted.
admin-archivos-comprobacion-fallida = The storage test failed. Check the server connection, credentials and read, write and delete permissions. Configuration was not changed.
forum-error-cargas-desactivadas = New file uploads are disabled. Published attachments remain available.
forum-error-limite-carga = The file must contain between 1 byte and { $limite } MiB.
forum-error-cuota-carga = You can keep up to { $cantidad } pending files and a total of { $limite } MiB per account.
